   "definition": "V3 (computed, toy; nothing from the networks). Lemma adam (e) escape time vs exact Adam on one gated coordinate.\nA frozen row's step-1 gap x (nats) falls by K per unit of weight motion (K = ||M_1||_1-like, 104-141). Its per-entry\nrestoring gradient grows as the cell rises: |g(x)| = g0 * exp(x0 - x) (gate e^{-gap}). Quasi-static ODE (the lemma):\ndx/dn = -lr*K*|g|/(|g| + eps)  ->  tau(X) = [(x0 - X) + e^{x0 - X} - 1]/(lr K), X = x0 - ln(eps/g0), then full speed.\nExact Adam (beta1 0.9, beta2 0.999, eps 1e-8, bias correction, fresh moments) on the same deterministic gradient.\nReported: updates until x <= 7.7 (c2's 'released' threshold), for the c2 settings (x0 = 14.5 median; g0 = beta * 1.3e-9\nper unit beta, the E1 per-entry rms of the bonus gradient at R3)."
  },
